  {
    "id": "e6be8df5aed3536b4560",
    "source": "Move a combatant on the battle map. A walk (no forced): an enemy taking its movement, or a character on their own turn, either an AI companion or a player character walking the move their player just declared; it spends their speed, stands them from prone for what standing costs, and draws opportunity attacks. A forced move (forced:true): a character pushed, pulled, or carried. A teleport (teleport:true): to a tile WITHOUT walking (Misty Step, a portal, a trap door), by spell with casterCharacterId for a character's (the server casts it and refuses a jump past its range), or casterEnemyId with enemyAbility (or spell) for an enemy's, or cause 'hazard'; the tile must be open and empty. The server enforces walls, occupancy, speed, and that a frightened creature never walks closer to what it fears; moves clamp to the farthest legal tile toward the target. A walking enemy passes through its allies' spaces and a character's two sizes apart at double cost (never stopping in one), and a Large or bigger one squeezes through a gap one size too small at double cost and is squeezing there (attacks against it have advantage).",
    "sourceHash": "e6be8df5aed3536b45603caf9b271bd6a79f86dcb475d560ddfeb5a182c5a5a0",
    "kinds": [
      "display-property"
    ],
    "sites": [
      {
        "file": "src/lib/dm/map-tools.ts",
        "line": 370
      }
    ]
  },
